      "seed": 834711417,
      "version": 342,
      "versionNonce": 865272025,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781241745215,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Django-Drf Tutorial\n\nNow lets learn how django drf works and we will build some \napi , most importantly we will learn how to interact with \ndb , how to serializer them (validate) , authentication \nand how to create a modular ui",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Django-Drf Tutorial\n\nNow lets learn how django drf works and we will build some \napi , most importantly we will learn how to interact with \ndb , how to serializer them (validate) , authentication \nand how to create a modular ui",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_u3J7dz73egyIVZR7FFXM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 321.1429138183594,
      "y": 370.50006103515625,
      "width": 1000.999755859375,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1158951799,
      "version": 266,
      "versionNonce": 202928505,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781242051349,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "let's learn a simple HTTP method what are they and how they work \nand from there we will move forward.\n\n1.Simple HTTP methods \n->Before touching the database let's understand how drf maps \nthe HTTP verbs to intent ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "let's learn a simple HTTP method what are they and how they work \nand from there we will move forward.\n\n1.Simple HTTP methods \n->Before touching the database let's understand how drf maps \nthe HTTP verbs to intent ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VLXKd2Ogfk_uUeN4EdEy2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 331.78582763671875,
      "y": 620.7857360839844,
      "width": 1036.9996337890625,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2059609913,
      "version": 261,
      "versionNonce": 1359625143,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1781242219749,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Verb     Meaning         Typical use\n-GET     Read            Fetch a resource or alist\n-POST    Create          Submit new data\n-PUT     Full replace    Replace an entire resource\n-PATCH   Partial update  Change one or two fields\n-DELETE  Remove          Delete a resource",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Verb     Meaning         Typical use\n-GET     Read            Fetch a resource or alist\n-POST    Create          Submit new data\n-PUT     Full replace    Replace an entire resource\n-PATCH   Partial update  Change one or two fields\n-DELETE  Remove          Delete a resource",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
